{"agent":"pv-log","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"`_bounded_events` only inspects the *immediate* values of the `data` mapping and only truncates them when they are `str`. Any large payload that is nested (`data = {\"payload\": {\"log\": \"A\"*100000}}` or `data = {\"chunks\": [\"A\"*100000, ...]}`) or that is itself a large non-string value is copied through verbatim, and `cut` stays `False`, so neither the in-string note nor `\"truncated\": true` is emitted. Concretely, given an event whose `data` is `{\"payload\": {\"log\": \"<100k chars>\"}}`, `--json` prints the full 100 000-character string with no indication that anything was omitted, so the acceptance criterion \"large payloads truncated with a note\" fails for exactly the payload shape (a blob nested under a key) that log events most often carry. The cap check needs to recurse into dict/list values (or at least measure the serialized field length) rather than only `isinstance(v, str)` at the top level.","digest":"60746652642be3f8","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/knowledge.py:_bounded_events","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/knowledge.py:_bounded_events"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":10419,"diff_sha":"ff80ce022f0179e9e20ac544f79df82a5eb7d00563cf7865e09713d7ab436fbd","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-view-log","elapsed_s":267.4,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/commands/knowledge.py:_bounded_events"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"critic","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e21d1cf46485331152b531c9f","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":11715,"schema":1,"subject":"B-view-log","ts":"2026-10-03T07:42:17.395200Z"}
{"agent":"pv-log","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The CLI stores `--agent` under the argparse destination `log_agent`, but the API filter added in this same change is the parameter `by_agent`. These are the only two places in the diff that touch the per-agent shard, and nothing connects them: the parser produces `args.log_agent`, while `history(..., by_agent=\"\")` only filters when `by_agent` is non-empty. So for the concrete input `ddflow history --agent alice`, `by_agent` stays `\"\"` (the default) and the list is not narrowed to alice's shard; if the dispatcher instead forwards the attribute by name (`by_agent=args.by_agent`), it is an `AttributeError`, since no `by_agent` attribute is ever set. Either the dest should be `by_agent`, or `cmd_history` must explicitly map `by_agent=args.log_agent`; as written the acceptance criterion \"--agent narrows to one shard\" is not satisfiable from the shown code.","digest":"768d6fead2c0e126","location":"ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:1276 (`--agent`, dest `log_agent`) / ddflow/api/knowledge.py:973 (`by_agent`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:1276 (`--agent`, dest `log_agent`) / ddflow/api/knowledge.py:973 (`by_agent`)"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":10419,"diff_sha":"ff80ce022f0179e9e20ac544f79df82a5eb7d00563cf7865e09713d7ab436fbd","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-view-log","elapsed_s":286.2,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2,3],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/cli.py:1276 (`--agent`, dest `log_agent`) / ddflow/api/knowledge.py:973 (`by_agent`)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"e3c5297e9db85a4ab3b026412","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":